d into the cumulative effect calculation is not explicitly stated in the report passages provided. The discrepancy between the stated £3,181.08 ongoing commitment and the calculated 1% of £327,945.44 (which would be £3,279.45) suggests either a rounding difference or a different calculation basis that is not explained. The vulnerability overlay: the client is recorded as having possible vulnerability due to recent divorce, employment change, and pending inheritance. The complexity of the charges structure (multiple layers, adviser fee separate from product charges, and the need to understand the combined impact) may not be adequately highlighted for a client in this position, particularly given the pending inheritance timing uncertainty and recent life events. However, the charges themselves are disclosed; the concern is whether the presentation and cumulative impact are sufficiently clear for a vulnerable client.","citations":[{"passageId":"P9","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"Annual recurring charges | Plan | Platform | Investment Management | Total Charge | Aviva Platform Personal Pension | 0.19% | 0.20% | 0.39% | £623.10 | £655.89 | £1,278.99","cells":null},{"passageId":"P10","source":"Anness, M Aviva pension charges 24.3.26.md","category":"H","quote":"Ongoing adviser charges | Product | Payable to | Paid | % of product wrapper value | Pension | Adviser | Monthly | 1.00%","cells":null},{"passageId":"P21","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"For researching, recommending and arranging these investments, we charge an initial advice fee of 3% of the amount invested as per the terms stated in our Client Agreement. In monetary terms this is 9,838.36 with current transfer values, this figure may fluctuate depending on transfer values. This will be paid directly by the pension scheme on transfer.","cells":null},{"passageId":"P8","source":"Suitability report 2026.md","category":"I","quote":"The charges quoted in this