wance is £60,000. If you take a flexi-access payment from your drawdown account this may trigger the money purchase annual allowance (MPAA). You'll still have an annual allowance of £60,000 in total, but no more than £10,000 can be paid into your defined contribution (money purchase) pensions and £50,000 for other pension investments. You can normally withdraw up to 25% of your pension fund as a tax-free lump sum. You may have to pay income tax on any income payments and lump sum payments you take. Both are treated as income, and therefore the tax you pay will depend on your personal circumstances.","cells":null}],"issueCategories":["Disclosure shortfall"],"severity":"Moderate","outcome":"PotentialConcern"}

